"The god who died at the Black Pyre was a god-tier fire serpent risen from the Depths."
"Its burned body lies beneath the Pyre, and its heart still beats once each night."
"The Black Pyre itself is the god's fused, blackened spine thrusting up from the earth."
"A shaft beside the god's body falls into an upper layer of the Depths."
"The Serpent of the Black Pyre is the god's last hatchling, grown fat on its dross."
"The Serpent coils around the shaft and guards the way down into the Depths."
"One who overcomes the Serpent may take its fire, the breath of the underworld."
"The Cursed City's undead priest gathers his Dross from the pools around the god's body."
